      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.\n\nThis dose adds up to 2,550 mg a day. That is the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, so it's within the limit but leaves no room to go higher. If this is a new start, many teams begin lower, for example 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg once daily, and increase slowly to limit GI side effects. You may want to confirm with your resident or attending that the full dose is what they intend.\n\nI went by the details you gave: normal kidney function and no allergies. Check that the eGFR is current, since metformin needs a dose change or should be stopped if renal function falls. Also hold it around iodinated contrast or acute illness."
      }
